# Shell scripts must be LF everywhere. A Windows checkout defaults to CRLF, and
# bash then reads `set -euo pipefail` as `set: pipefail\r: invalid option name`
# and exits 1 -- the script fails before it runs a single useful line. Git for
# Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this the packaging scripts only
# work on the machine that wrote them.
*.sh text eol=lf
